From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MIRAGE <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:13:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] MIRAGE: getent, tty and ss

Three programs typed early on a host that has just been entered, none of
which stock Cowrie has. Each answers from what the session can already
see another way, so the answers agree:

- getent (glibc 2.36) from the session's own /etc files: passwd, group,
  shadow and gshadow (root's), hosts and ahosts with the files backend's
  ways (the IPv6 loopback given as 127.0.0.1 when the files are listed,
  IPv6 first for a name), services, protocols, networks. A host name no
  file holds is declined to the gate; run all the same it finds nothing.
- tty (coreutils 9.1): the terminal when the session has one and nothing
  is piped in.
- ss (iproute2 6.1) for internet sockets: what the deployment's process
  list says listens ([mirage] processes, key sockets), and the session's
  own connection. The processes named are the ones ps shows, newest
  first; root sees every holder, anyone else their own. The table is laid
  out by ss's own rule, piped and on a terminal of any width. Other
  socket families and per-socket details are declined.

Texts and layouts are held to recordings from the reference host and a
real Debian 12 guest (test/mirage_ss_reference.json).
